Thu Sep  3 08:52:46 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 1.18.27:
  * Default the provider header and streamed-chunk timeouts to
    five minutes instead of leaving them unset; both take false
    to disable.
  * Bind Anthropic thinking blocks only on Claude 5.1 and newer,
    so older deployments stop rejecting the request, and honour
    blockBinding: false as a per-provider opt-out.
  * Catch the rejection from cancelling a timed-out SSE read
    instead of leaving it unhandled.
- Retrace the vendor keep list (507 to 509 store entries):
  ai-gateway-provider 3.2.0 and gitlab-ai-provider 6.12.1 are now
  each kept twice, one entry per @ai-sdk/provider-utils peer
  resolution (4.0.23 and 4.0.50). Same 506 packages, same SPDX
  set, still no copyleft; README.SUSE-maint records the audit as
  redone for 1.18.27.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Sep  2 07:07:03 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 1.18.26:
  * Tolerate stale thinking blocks in Claude 5 sessions instead of
    failing the request after a prompt or tool change.
  * Accept "none" reasoning effort on Bedrock GPT-5.6 models.
  * Fix Amazon Bedrock reasoning and replay handling.
  * Keep tool call timing accurate when a tool updates its
    metadata while it is still running.
  * Stop apply_patch emitting an empty move path in permission
    metadata.
  * Ask for the resource name directly during Azure CLI sign-in
    instead of querying the Azure management APIs.
  * Keep the home screen shortcuts right-aligned when no session
    is open.
- Retrace the vendor keep list (512 to 507 store entries):
  @ai-sdk/anthropic collapses to a single 3.0.111 through a new
  root override, amazon-bedrock moves to 4.0.166, and seroval
  falls out with the solid-js/web import the TUI dropped. SPDX
  set unchanged over 506 packages, still no copyleft; the audit
  is recorded in README.SUSE-maint.
- Dropping seroval 1.3.2 also takes CVE-2026-23736,
  CVE-2026-23737, CVE-2026-23956, CVE-2026-23957, CVE-2026-24006
  and CVE-2026-59940 out of the bundled tree. Incidental, not an
  upstream security fix.

